/**
 * Grade 2 — Mika's step up from grade 1, which topped out at 20 with no number above it
 * in any of its 150 questions. Two topics, mirroring the shape of "חיבור עד 10" /
 * "חיסור עד 10" in `grade1.ts`: one style each, so `hasStyleLessons` keeps them on the
 * plain level screen rather than a style picker, exactly like those two already work.
 *
 * `easy` stays clear of regrouping so the new range (not the mechanic) is what's new;
 * `medium` moves to two two-digit numbers, still without regrouping; `hard` requires
 * carrying (addition) or borrowing (subtraction) on every question — the actual new
 * skill, not just bigger numbers. Every question carries a literal `steps`: the generic
 * explanation `explain.ts` would otherwise compute for bare arithmetic works off "round to
 * the nearest ten," a different method than the tens/units column method these hints
 * teach — shown together, hint and solution would contradict each other. Written steps
 * keep both speaking the same method, column by column, with an explicit carried or
 * borrowed ten where the hint says one happens.
 *
 * Style ids are written as plain strings, never imported from `style.ts` — same
 * circular-import reason `grade1.ts` does this; a test checks both directions instead.
 */
